            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " signals that the annotated test class is disabled in Spring AOT (ahead-of-time) mode, which means that the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for the test class will not be processed for AOT optimizations at build time."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "If a test class is annotated with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@DisabledInAotMode"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", all other test classes which specify configuration to load the same "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " must also be annotated with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@DisabledInAotMode"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". Failure to annotate all such test classes will result in an exception, either at build time or run time."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When used with JUnit Jupiter based tests, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@DisabledInAotMode"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " also signals that the annotated test class or test method is disabled when running the test suite in Spring AOT mode. When applied at the class level, all test methods within that class will be disabled. In this sense, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@DisabledInAotMode"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " has semantics similar to those of JUnit Jupiter’s "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@DisabledInNativeImage"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
